+# Free-Text Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope; Narrowing by Specialty Is In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners the only searchable entity. Like every other row derived in the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, it was written from observed absence, so it read wider than any decision behind it.
+
+The owner has now asked for the veterinarian directory to be narrowed to a single specialty, on both the page and the machine-readable form. That request meets NG-9 head on: read at its widest, the row forbids it. The owner decided the row at intake (2026-08-10):
+
+> NG-9 is narrowed. Free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Read NG-9 at its widest and decline the request.** Rejected: the owner's decision is explicit, and the row's own rationale is about not repeating paged prefix search, which narrowing to one specialty does not do.
+2. **Drop NG-9 entirely.** Rejected: it would open free-text search over pets, visits, and veterinarians — three surfaces nobody asked for, each repeating what owner search already demonstrates.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen). The row keeps its reason and loses only the reading that covered filtering on an attribute the directory already puts on the page.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian. It does not cover narrowing a listing by an attribute that listing already shows. Narrowing the veterinarian directory to one specialty is in scope, recorded as `REQ-VET-004`.
+
+The line is the input, not the entity. Free text typed against a name is search and stays out. A value chosen from a closed set the directory already displays is filtering and is in.
+
+A further request to search veterinarians by name, or to search pets or visits at all, still needs its own recorded owner decision. This narrowing does not reopen those.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation as a decided row, alongside NG-4 and NG-5. Every other row remains part of it.
+- The veterinarian directory gains its first read capability beyond listing. The machine-readable form, withdrawn as `REQ-VET-002` on 2026-07-31, returns as a supported surface under `REQ-VET-003` and carries the same narrowing.
+- Filtering another listing by an attribute it already shows now has a precedent to argue from, and no fresh non-goal question.
+- The directory page gains no visible control in this round. Whether it should is an open question, not a settled non-goal.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-004) — the capability the narrowing admits.
