+### Veterinarian directory URL contract
+
+This section is owner-stated rather than read off the code. It is the one place in this document where the design is authoritative and the source follows it. The requirements it serves are `REQ-VET-003` and `REQ-VET-004` in [prd.md](prd.md#req-vet-004); the scope decision behind them is [ADR 2026-08-10](adr/2026-08-10-non-goal-veterinarian-search-narrowed.md).
+
+- `/vets.html?specialty=<name>` lists only veterinarians holding that specialty. Paging applies to the narrowed list, and every pagination link on the page carries the parameter.
+- `/vets?specialty=<name>` returns only those veterinarians in the machine-readable form.
+- The value is matched against the whole specialty name, without regard to letter case. A value matching only the beginning of a name matches nothing.
+- A specialty no veterinarian holds yields the ordinary page or document with an empty veterinarian list, under HTTP 200.
+- An empty or all-space value behaves as an absent parameter.
+- Without the parameter, both routes behave as they did before `REQ-VET-004`.
+- Neither surface carries a form, dropdown, or other page control for the narrowing.
